# EtAssetInfo Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtAssetInfo` is a compound UI component for rendering an asset/person identity block with:

- Avatar/logo
- Primary text (`Title`)
- Secondary text (`Subtitle`)

It supports two layouts:

- `horizontal`: avatar on the left, title/subtitle stacked on the right
- `vertical`: avatar, then title, then subtitle in a column

This component is intentionally presentational. It does not manage fetching, navigation, selection state, or business logic.

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtAssetInfo` (main component)

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo
  data={{
    avatar?: {
      source: string,                  // required when using EtAssetInfo.Avatar
      size?: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large', // default: 'medium'
      shape?: 'circle' | 'square',         // default: 'square'
      alt?: string,
    },
    title?: string,                         // used when Title has no children
    subtitle?: string,                     // used when Subtitle has no children
  }}
  layout?: 'horizontal' | 'vertical'       // default: 'horizontal'
  ellipsizeMode?: 'head' | 'middle' | 'tail' | 'clip'  // default: 'tail'
  maxWidth?: number                        // horizontal layout only; constrains text block
  shrink?: boolean                         // horizontal layout; fills flex parent and shrinks text block for proper ellipsis
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
>
  {children}
</EtAssetInfo>
```

- `layout`, `ellipsizeMode`, `maxWidth`, and `shrink` are **root-level props**.
- `data.title` and `data.subtitle` are optional; when set, `<EtAssetInfo.Title />` and `<EtAssetInfo.Subtitle />` can be used with no children to render that text.

`children` are expected to be compound subcomponents:

- `<EtAssetInfo.Avatar />`
- `<EtAssetInfo.Title>...</EtAssetInfo.Title>`
- `<EtAssetInfo.Subtitle>...</EtAssetInfo.Subtitle>`

### `EtAssetInfo.Avatar`

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo.Avatar style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> />
```

- Reads `avatar` config from context (no direct avatar props).
- Throws at runtime if `avatar.source` is missing/empty.
- Uses internal `EtAvatar` with `EtAvatar.Image`.

### `EtAssetInfo.Title`

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo.Title>{ReactNode}</EtAssetInfo.Title>
```

- Delegates to internal `EtAssetInfoText` with `value={data.title}`, `variant="label-primary-bold"`, and theme color for text.
- **No children and no `data.title`**: renders `null`.
- **No children but `data.title` is set**: renders `EtText` with `data.title`, `numberOfLines={1}`, and `ellipsizeMode` from context.
- **Has children**: renders a horizontal row wrapper (`View`) for custom composition (e.g. label + badge).
- No `style` prop; styling is driven by variant and theme.

### `EtAssetInfo.Subtitle`

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo.Subtitle>{ReactNode}</EtAssetInfo.Subtitle>
```

- Delegates to internal `EtAssetInfoText` with `value={data.subtitle}` and `variant="label-secondary-regular"`.
- **No children and no `data.subtitle`**: renders `null`.
- **No children but `data.subtitle` is set**: renders `EtText` with `data.subtitle`, `numberOfLines={1}`, and `ellipsizeMode` from context.
- **Has children**: renders a horizontal row wrapper (`View`) for custom composition.
- No `style` prop; styling is driven by variant.

## Internal Architecture

### 1) Data normalization (`useDefaults`)

`useDefaults({ data, layout, ellipsizeMode, maxWidth })` resolves defaults and returns a memoized context value of type `EtAssetDefaults`:

- `layout`: defaults to `'horizontal'`
- `ellipsizeMode`: defaults to `'tail'`
- `maxWidth`: passed through only when layout is horizontal; set to `undefined` in vertical layout
- `data`: spread from input; `data.avatar` is normalized to `{ source, shape: shape ?? 'square', size: size ?? 'medium' }` when present (other avatar fields such as `alt` are not merged into this normalized object in the current implementation)

### 2) Child slot extraction (`useSlots`)

`useSlots(children)` scans children by `displayName` and extracts slots:

- `EtAssetInfo.Avatar`
- `EtAssetInfo.Title`
- `EtAssetInfo.Subtitle`

Important behavior:

- If multiple components of the same slot exist, the last one wins.
- Unknown children are ignored by the slotter.
- Slot order in JSX is not required; render order is controlled by root layout logic.

### 3) Title and Subtitle rendering (`EtAssetInfoText`)

`EtAssetInfoTitle` and `EtAssetInfoSubtitle` delegate to a shared internal component `EtAssetInfoText`, which:

- If `children` is present: renders a horizontal row `View` with `X2` gap (custom composition).
- Else if `value` is present: renders `EtText` with `variant`, `numberOfLines={1}`, `ellipsizeMode` from context, and optional `style` (used only by the internal call; Title passes theme color, Subtitle uses default).
- Otherwise: returns `null`.

Title passes `value={data.title}`, `variant="label-primary-bold"`, and theme `color: colors.textPrimaryNeutral`. Subtitle passes `value={data.subtitle}` and `variant="label-secondary-regular"`. Both use a fixed `lineHeight: 20` for the text style.

### 4) Context boundary

`EtAssetInfo` provides `EtAssetInfoContext`, and subcomponents read it via `useEtAssetInfoContext()`.

- Using subcomponents outside `EtAssetInfo` throws runtime errors.

### 5) Layout rendering

- `horizontal`: renders `avatar` + text block (`title` + `subtitle`), with optional `maxWidth` style on text block.
- `vertical`: renders `avatar`, `title`, `subtitle` sequentially.
- Root container always uses design-system spacing (`X2`) and `alignSelf: 'flex-start'`.
- When `shrink` is `true` (horizontal only): the root container becomes `flex: 1` and the text block becomes `flex: 1, minWidth: 0`. This makes `EtAssetInfo` claim the available row space and lets `Title`/`Subtitle` shrink so `numberOfLines={1}` produces a proper ellipsis. Useful when the parent is a flex row with siblings (e.g. price) that should keep their natural width.

## Usage Patterns

### Data-driven title and subtitle (empty slots)

When `data.title` and `data.subtitle` are set, use empty slots so text and ellipsis are driven by context:

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo
  data={{
    avatar: {
      source: user.avatarUrl,
      shape: 'circle',
      size: 'medium',
      alt: user.name,
    },
    title: user.name,
    subtitle: `@${user.username}`,
  }}
  layout="horizontal"
>
  <EtAssetInfo.Avatar />
  <EtAssetInfo.Title />
  <EtAssetInfo.Subtitle />
</EtAssetInfo>
```

### Asset list row with truncation width

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo
  data={{
    avatar: {
      source: asset.logoUrl,
      shape: 'square',
      size: 'medium',
      alt: asset.symbol,
    },
    title: asset.symbol,
    subtitle: asset.name,
  }}
  layout="horizontal"
  maxWidth={140}
  ellipsizeMode="tail"
>
  <EtAssetInfo.Avatar />
  <EtAssetInfo.Title />
  <EtAssetInfo.Subtitle />
</EtAssetInfo>
```

### Dynamic truncation in a flex row (with sibling price)

Use `shrink` when `EtAssetInfo` shares a row with siblings whose width changes at runtime (e.g. a live price). The text block fills the remaining space and truncates with an ellipsis automatically — no `maxWidth` magic number needed.

```tsx
<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: X4 }}>
  <EtAssetInfo
    data={{
      avatar: { source: asset.logoUrl, shape: 'square', size: 'medium' },
      title: asset.symbol,
      subtitle: asset.name,
    }}
    shrink
  >
    <EtAssetInfo.Avatar />
    <EtAssetInfo.Title />
    <EtAssetInfo.Subtitle />
  </EtAssetInfo>

  <View>{/* price section keeps its natural width */}</View>
</View>
```

Prefer `shrink` over a hardcoded `maxWidth` when available space is dynamic.

### Custom title/subtitle (children with badges)

When you need custom composition (e.g. badge next to title), pass children and omit title/subtitle from `data`:

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo data={{ avatar: { source: asset.logoUrl, shape: 'square', size: 'medium' } }} layout="horizontal">
  <EtAssetInfo.Avatar />
  <EtAssetInfo.Title>
    <EtText variant="label-primary-bold">{asset.symbol}</EtText>
    <EtBadge color="green">
      <EtBadge.Label>100</EtBadge.Label>
    </EtBadge>
  </EtAssetInfo.Title>
  <EtAssetInfo.Subtitle>{asset.name}</EtAssetInfo.Subtitle>
</EtAssetInfo>
```

### Vertical card identity block

```tsx
<EtAssetInfo
  data={{
    avatar: {
      source: asset.logoUrl,
      shape: 'square',
      size: 'large',
      alt: asset.symbol,
    },
    title: asset.symbol,
    subtitle: asset.name,
  }}
  layout="vertical"
>
  <EtAssetInfo.Avatar />
  <EtAssetInfo.Title />
  <EtAssetInfo.Subtitle />
</EtAssetInfo>
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using subcomponents outside root provider

```tsx
// BAD - throws at runtime
<EtAssetInfo.Title>BTC</EtAssetInfo.Title>
```

Fix: Always render subcomponents inside `<EtAssetInfo>...</EtAssetInfo>`.

### ❌ Missing avatar source

```tsx
// BAD - Avatar throws because source is empty/missing
<EtAssetInfo data={{ title: 'BTC' }}>
  <EtAssetInfo.Avatar />
</EtAssetInfo>
```

Fix: Provide `data.avatar.source` whenever using `EtAssetInfo.Avatar`.

### ❌ Assuming arbitrary children are rendered

```tsx
// BAD - random children are ignored by slot extraction
<EtAssetInfo data={data}>
  <View />
</EtAssetInfo>
```

Fix: Use the supported compound subcomponents for visible output.

### ❌ Hardcoded spacing/color overrides as default approach

Fix: Prefer design tokens (`X2`) and theme-driven text styling via built-in Title/Subtitle behavior. Use `style` props only for targeted overrides.

## Dependencies & Design System Integration

- Theme:
  - `EtAssetInfoTitle` uses `useEtoroTheme().colors.textPrimaryNeutral` for data-driven title text (via `EtAssetInfoText`).
- Typography:
  - Title: `label-primary-bold` (through `EtAssetInfoText`)
  - Subtitle: `label-secondary-regular` (through `EtAssetInfoText`)
- Primitives:
  - Avatar rendering uses `EtAvatar` + `EtAvatar.Image`.
  - Title/Subtitle data-driven text and row layout use internal `EtAssetInfoText` (which uses `EtText` and `View`).
- Spacing:
  - Uses `X2` token in root and in `EtAssetInfoText` row wrapper.

